  - LinuxUnixPlatform, RedHatEnterpriseLinuxPlatform, SuseLinuxPlatform, WindowsPlatform,
    WindowsWithSqlServerPlatform, WindowsWithSqlServerEnterprisePlatform,
    WindowsWithSqlServerStandardPlatform, WindowsWithSqlServerWebPlatform
  - Each should have a string value equal to its canonical label, e.g.
    LinuxUnixPlatform -> 'Linux/UNIX'
    RedHatEnterpriseLinuxPlatform -> 'Red Hat Enterprise Linux'
    SuseLinuxPlatform -> 'SUSE Linux'
    WindowsPlatform -> 'Windows'
    WindowsWithSqlServerPlatform -> 'Windows with SQL Server'
    WindowsWithSqlServerEnterprisePlatform -> 'Windows with SQL Server Enterprise'
    WindowsWithSqlServerStandardPlatform -> 'Windows with SQL Server Standard'
    WindowsWithSqlServerWebPlatform -> 'Windows with SQL Server Web'
  - A deprecated set of constants with the same values:
    LinuxUnixPlatformDeprecated, RedHatEnterpriseLinuxPlatformDeprecated, etc.

- A Node.js verifier at scripts/verify-platforms.js that:
  - Reads src/instance-platforms.ts as text and extracts all exported constants from both the new set and the deprecated set.
  - Verifies that each new constant value matches its canonical label.
  - Verifies that each deprecated constant value equals the corresponding new constant’s value.
  - Writes a logs/verify.log with a timestamped report including per-constant entries and a final OK line when all checks pass.

How to run
